{"shortDescription":"Kansai Electric Power TSE:9503 shut its 826-megawatt No. 3 reactor at the Mihama nuclear power station in western Japan on Friday after water droplets were detected in a high-pressure turbine feedwater heater, a company spokesperson said.The company manually shut down the reactor for safety checks…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Kansai Electric Power ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TSE:9503","text":"TSE:9503"}}," shut its 826-megawatt No. 3 reactor at the Mihama nuclear power station in western Japan on Friday after water droplets were detected in a high-pressure turbine feedwater heater, a company spokesperson said."]},{"type":"p","children":["The company manually shut down the reactor for safety checks. It had restarted it last Saturday and had been offline since May for maintenance following a technical problem."]},{"type":"p","children":["Kansai has not set a schedule for restarting the reactor, the spokesperson said."]},{"type":"p","children":["As of Friday, Japan has 11 nuclear reactors in operation, with a combined capacity of 10,553 MW."]},{"type":"p","children":["Many utilities are undergoing re-licensing to meet stricter safety standards implemented after the 2011 Fukushima disaster. Before the disaster, Japan operated a total of 54 reactors."]},{"type":"p","children":["The table below shows the status of Japan's nuclear power plants."]},{"type":"p","children":["The regional utilities are: Chubu Electric Power ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TSE:9502","text":"TSE:9502"}},", Chugoku Electric Power ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TSE:9504","text":"TSE:9504"}},", Hokkaido Electric Power ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TSE:9509","text":"TSE:9509"}},", Hokuriku Electric Power ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TSE:9505","text":"TSE:9505"}},", Kansai Electric Power ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TSE:9503","text":"TSE:9503"}},", Kyushu Electric Power ",{"type":"sym